## Re-executed after a sandbox rebuild (same commit tree, 2026-09-02, later in the session)

The sandbox was rebuilt mid-session and its git pointer rolled back to `86eaaae2` while the pushed work
was intact; the checkout was reset to `f7815e473` and the gates re-run from a clean venv. Same numbers:

```
$ tsc -p src/tsconfig.pulseai-check.json --noEmit                 # strict, scoped
Pulse errors: 0     total error lines: 364 (missing @types, environmental)     pulseai files in program: 26
$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest <7 desktop/branding/overlay/boundary files> -q
38 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed          # 22 skips = lanes needing esbuild, at that moment
$ npm install --no-save esbuild && pytest test_pulse_session_registration_parity.py test_hermes_activity_parity.py -q
15 passed, 1 skipped                      # the 8 projection tests execute in node again
```

The 1 skip is `test_hermes_activity_parity.py` needing the pinned `~/.hermes-ref` checkout, which a rebuilt
container does not carry. Still unproven here: build, paint, and anything on Windows.
